<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Umberto II</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1904">1904</a>–<a href="/years/1983">1983</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Umberto II of Italy</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Umberto II was the last King of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a>, reigning for just over a month in 1946. The son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/victor-emmanuel-iii">Victor Emmanuel III</a>, he acted as lieutenant-general of the realm from 1944 and became king when his father abdicated on 9 May 1946. After the referendum of 2 June 1946 voted for a republic he left for exile in Portugal, earning the nickname King of May.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/umberto-ii.jpg" alt="Umberto II" width="320" height="378" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Tanner (Capt), War Office official photographer · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Umberto_II,_1944.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
